WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
A reaction has two reactants.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.090
Double the concentration of the first,
and the rate goes up four times.

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.410
Double the concentration of the second,
and the rate doesn't change at all.

4
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:16.430
The same change, made to each in turn,
gives completely different results.

5
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.970
So what does that tell
you about the reaction?

6
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.350
In this mission, you'll
write rate equations,

7
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.930
and meet the order of a reaction
with respect to each reactant.

8
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.530
You'll find orders from initial-rate data,

9
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.690
and work out the units
of the rate constant.

10
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.080
Your mission: work out what the two
results reveal about the reaction.
